Test fixtures: sources and licences

Everything in this folder is used only by the tests. None of it is installed with Fluentfolio.

audio/ls_4446_*.opus
  42 utterances of speaker 4446 from LibriSpeech test-clean.
  LibriSpeech ASR corpus, Vassil Panayotov, Guoguo Chen, Daniel Povey and Sanjeev Khudanpur, 2015.
  https://www.openslr.org/12
  Licence: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Changes: level raised to at least -20 dBFS active speech (peak at most -6 dBFS), cut to the speech with 100 ms
  around it, silences under -55 dBFS longer than 100 ms shortened to 100 ms, a -75 dBFS dither added, and
  re-encoded as 16 kHz mono Ogg Opus. The texts in audio/clips.json are the corpus transcripts.

audio/*.opus (all other files)
  Speech synthesised for these tests with Kokoro-82M (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, revision
  f3ff3571), voices bf_emma, bm_george, af_bella, af_heart and ef_dora.
  Licence of the model and voices: Apache-2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  The texts were written for these tests and carry the licence of this repository.
  Changes: resampled from 24 kHz to 16 kHz, then the same level, cut, silence, dither and Opus steps as above.

audio/clips.json
  Each clip's text, its reference syllable count, its source and its licence. Syllable counts come from
  eSpeak NG phones (en-us, one word at a time, one syllable per vowel phone), with hand counts for six words where
  eSpeak NG joins two vowels or spells letters: area, museum, tedious, theatre, mm, hmm.

evidence/*.json
  Fluentfolio's own evidence files from two composed sessions built from the clips above: CS-SOLO, with a
  learner transcript made from its texts, and CS-SWAP. The words in them are those clips' texts as the speech
  model heard them, under the licences given above.

sessions/*.json
  Recipes written for these tests. tests/support/session_builder.py builds each one into a 16 kHz WAV and a
  truth.json at test time; generated sessions are never committed.

Tones, noise and other synthetic signals are generated by the tests at run time.
Larger public data is listed in tests/data_manifest.toml, each file with its licence and credit line: the whole
of LibriSpeech test-clean and the VOiCES clip (CC-BY-4.0), the test split of speechocean762 (CC-BY-4.0), six
shards of EdAcc (CC-BY-SA-4.0), and the dev and test splits of the Nyra Disfluency Speech English set
(Apache-2.0). tools/fetch_test_data.py downloads it; it is never committed.
